  out   where the consensus is copied
  R     the consensus
  ix    the flat positions `0 .. N-1`

sw_run3_num  @34df77ae
  what  Run every member of a registry whose members return one number, and
        return the median of their answers, with the dissent recorded in
        `rep`; with `release` set, return member `0`'s answer alone.
  why   Scalar stages (an energy, a norm) need the same check as array stages;
        a one-column table lets them share `sw_table_median`
        [test "the scalar and (nmax, x) drivers take medians too"].
  ms       the registry: members `(Arr, Arr, Arr) -> number`
  x1       the first input
  x2       the second input
  x3       the third input
  rep      the report to fill
  release  `1` to run member `0` alone
  nstrat   how many members the registry has
  T        the table, one row per member and one column
  m        the member being run
  C        the median, one entry

sweep3_num  @cfbdd291
  what  Run a registry of scalar-valued members and assert that they agree to
