  x3    the third input
  tol   the largest relative deviation that counts as agreement
  rep   the report to fill
  out   `out[0]` receives the median

sw_runnx_arr  @ef07bdb3
  what  Run every member of a registry with the Boys function's signature,
        `(nmax, x) -> Arr` (values for orders `0 .. nmax` at one argument), and
        return the elementwise median, with the dissent recorded in `rep`; with
        `release` set, return member `0`'s result alone.
  why   The Boys function has several implementations (series, asymptotic
        form, tables), and this is their signature. Its inputs are numbers, so
        no copies are needed.
  ms       the registry: members `(nmax, x) -> Arr`
  nmax     the highest order wanted
  x        the argument
  N        how many entries a result has, `nmax + 1`
  ncmp     how many leading entries are compared
  rep      the report to fill
  release  `1` to run member `0` alone
  nstrat   how many members the registry has
  ix       the flat positions `0 .. N-1`
  T        the table of results, one row per member
  out      member `0`'s result, overwritten by the consensus
  m        the member being run
  cur      member m's result
  C        the consensus

