  cov    the coverage table, `[nclass, SW_COV_NSTRAT]`
  cls    the class that was checked
  strat  the strategy that checked it

sw_cov_nstrat  @c327565c
  cov   the coverage table
  cls   the class asked about
  n     how many strategies have a nonzero count for it
  s     the strategy being looked at

sw_cov_covered  @6c862043
  cov   the coverage table
  n     how many classes have at least one strategy
  c     the class being looked at

sw_cov_min_strat  @6f25d7da
  why   The gate's quantity: the weakest-checked class decides whether the
        build's coverage is enough.
  cov   the coverage table
  best  the fewest strategies found so far behind a covered class
  c     the class being looked at
  k     how many strategies checked class c

sw_cov_gate  @b7ef6e4f
  why   One strategy agreeing with itself proves nothing; a class counts as
        checked only when at least two independent strategies were compared on
        it [test "coverage counts strategies per class and gates on at least two"].
  cov   the coverage table

sw_cov_report  @b5a96dc6
  cov       the coverage table
  c         the class being reported
  k         how many strategies checked it
  hits      how many checks it had in total
  s         the strategy being added up
  coverage  the line shown: class, strategies, total checks

sw_cls_eri  @c23c2fd2
  why   An integral $(ab|cd)$ has the same value under swapping a with b, c with
        d, and the two pairs, so the eight orderings are one class of work;
        counting them apart would split one class's coverage over eight rows
        [test "ERI classes are canonical under the 8-fold symmetry"].
  la    the angular momentum of the first function
  lb    of the second
  lc    of the third
  ld    of the fourth
  a     the larger l of the bra pair
  b     the smaller l of the bra pair
  c     the larger l of the ket pair
  d     the smaller l of the ket pair
  bra   the bra pair as one index
  ket   the ket pair as one index

sw_cls_boys  @a57b522c
  why   The Boys function's implementations switch methods by argument (series
        for small x, asymptotic form for large x), so coverage must be counted
        per argument range as well as per order.
  n     the order
  x     the argument
  edges the upper edge of each argument range but the last
  bin   which argument range x falls in

